EE-to-IOP SIF commands: the EE sceSifSendCmd delivers the packet to the IOP module's handler.
Why: the IOP sifcmd services sceSifAddCmdHandler/RemoveCmdHandler/SetCmdBuffer/SetSysCmdBuffer were no-ops and
the EE sceSifSendCmd only returned success (reading args 5/6 from the stack instead of t0/t1 and copying the
extra data within EE RAM). FMOD.IRX's EE<->IOP command channel never answered: Jackass waited forever on its
reply semaphore (0x2FE840) under the loading bar. Now: the IOP handlers are recorded (with the module gp), the
EE call DMAs the extra data into IOP RAM, fills the SIF header and runs handler(packet, data) on the emulated
IOP after catching it up to EE time, the same path EE-to-IOP RPC takes.
Origin: this project (jackass-ps2-recomp), 2026-10-27.

